<title>INDIA: India Essar may cut Ratna stake later.</title>
<headline>India Essar may cut Ratna stake later.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Essar Oil may sell part of its 50-percent stake in the Ratna oilfield development venture once a production sharing contract (PSC) has been signed, a senior company official told Reuters on Monday.</p>
<p>The official, who declined to be named, denied a newspaper report that Britain's Premier Oil Plc was seeking to cut or sell all of its 10-percent stake in the venture.</p>
<p>He said Premier had in fact approached Essar, asking to buy part of the Indian company's share, if it was up for sale.</p>
</text>
